# Xquik Product Signals

Use Xquik as source-backed public X data input for product decisions.

## Source Truth
- Docs: https://docs.xquik.com/api-reference/overview
- OpenAPI: https://xquik.com/openapi.json
- MCP: https://docs.xquik.com/mcp/overview

## Flow
1. State product question
2. Map to framework: `business-product-leadership`, `diffusion-release-tracking`, `product-analytics`, or `product-ux-research`
3. Select signal: account, keyword, post, conversation, launch term, competitor term, or event
4. Verify endpoint or MCP tool in source truth
5. Define sample window, terms, inclusion rules, exclusion rules
6. Separate observations from interpretation
7. Recommend go, hold, or research more

## Guardrails
- Keep Xquik opt-in
- Require explicit approval for private, write, scheduled, persistent, or bulk workflows
- Do not store raw public content beyond task need unless asked
- Do not treat social volume as product-market fit by itself
- Do not support harassment, evasion, or personal targeting
